      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It happened again last night. I never switched worlds, I basically stayed in the same place for 5 hours. These are the final logs in the log file before systemd killed the process. Memory usage over time is not logged because I'm not switching worlds.\n\n2026.07.25 22:41:50 Debug      -  [Behaviour] OnPlayerLeftRoom\n\n2026.07.25 22:41:50 Debug      -  [Behaviour] OnPlayerLeft Murphite (edited out ID)\n\n2026.07.25 22:41:50 Debug      -  Removed player Murphite\n\n2026.07.25 22:41:50 Debug      -  [Behaviour] Destroying Murphite\n\nsystemd log:\n\nJul 25 22:42:34 nibl-linux kernel: Memory cgroup out of memory: Killed process 36602 (VRChat.exe) total-vm:85154820kB, anon-rss:39261664kB, file-rss:406132kB, shmem-rss:65144kB, UID:1000 pgtables:82144kB oom_score_adj:200\n\nI don't think it's something I'm doing. I think it's somebody's avatar or something like that. Something I can't reproduce myself. Because I was literally AFK tabbed out in an idle game world when it triggered OOM. There's days where I can go two days there without this happening, but tonight only lasted 5 hours. I wish I could help diagnose this more but I don't have any clues. My own actions aren't causing it. I'm not doing anything different from the days where it goes 2 days straight just fine.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
