      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I managed to capture definitive proof of the memory leak in action. I began logging the process as soon as I noticed the memory usage climbing and captured continuous memory statistics and smap, pmap, and lsof snapshots at several points during the leak. Hopefully you (the devs) can use this to finally pin it down. My VRChat game log is also included. You can probably line them up to see what caused the leak.\n\nAfter switching to another world, RSS did not return to normal. It remained at around 30.8 GB with 30.4 GB of it dirty. The snapshot immediately before the world change was 30.0 GB RSS. I let it go for a bit longer before hopping worlds. Some virtual address space was released, but the committed anonymous memory was retained until the client was closed.\n\nEdit: The order of the logs in pairs of three is initial -> later -> final, with the logs labeled 'final' occurring AFTER I switched to my home world and 'later' occurring a bit before that. It's also worth noting that switching worlds did stop the leak.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
