      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "69e1109614916839a1a48a59",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I upped the limit another 10GB to 48GB because I'd be more AFK those days and wanted more time to catch it, yet the game leaked out and crashed three times in one night and it was always soon after I had to step away for a few hours every time and not during the few hours I was there to monitor it. However, after turning on safe mode and idling in the same instance after the third OOM crash, the memory leak stopped occurring. It's something on someone's avatar, not something in the world.\n\nNext time it happens I'll use the in game debug menu to capture more info. I didn't know it existed until very recently.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
